    <string name="tutorial_swipe">Swipe down on a settings page when it is scrolled to the top to reveal the live LED preview and bring controls within reach. Swipe up, or press Back, to close it. Swipe left or right to change tabs. You can reopen this guide from Settings → Tutorial.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_test">Tap the floating Test pill, then press the power button to lock the device. With notification access and screen-off lighting enabled, Glow LED waits briefly, then shows the black notification screen. Swipe-down preview lets you try styles without locking the device.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_setup">Open the Setup cards to enable notification access and either Display over other apps or Accessibility. Accessibility can also switch the screen off immediately. On Xiaomi and other strict devices, check autostart and battery restrictions. The progress bar shows which required permissions remain.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_styles">Style offers 11 animations, including Twin orbit and Sparkle. Choose a colour, speed, size, glow and multi-app mode. Camera position adjusts the ring around your camera. App theme and haptic feedback are in the Settings tab; they never change the black notification background.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_transfers">When an app posts a progress notification, the ring shows how far the transfer has got, with a small arrow on the bottom of the ring: ↑ upload, ↓ download, ↕ direction unknown. Moving progress with no percentage uses a spinner. Use app colours, or choose upload/download colours in Screen on. Transfers without a progress notification cannot be detected.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_battery" formatted="false">While charging, the ring fills with your battery level in your low, medium and high colours, with a small bolt on the bottom of the ring that glows each time the battery gains a percent. Plugging in while the phone is locked shows it for a few seconds; transfers take priority. Battery % below the ring is optional (Screen on → Charging &amp; battery).</string>
    <string name="tutorial_messages">On the black notification screen, tap an app icon to read its notification, reply or mark it as read when the app supports those actions. Reply may require unlocking. Double-tap to reveal the lock screen. Alerts controls allowed apps, per-app colours, silent notifications and Do Not Disturb.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_power">The screen-off view wakes the display and draws black; it is not the device’s native hardware AOD. Black pixels switch off on OLED, but LCD backlights can still glow. Battery offers quiet hours, low-battery protection, frame-rate limits and motion reminders. Settings also contains backup, restore, language and the event log.</string>
